lines=['# Final standard-autograd embedding component results','', 'The completed standard-autograd owner measures **2.554 ms versus 13.040 ms** for fixture component forward + backward. Absolute allocated peak is **5,781,722,112 versus 8,950,373,888 bytes**. These are component measurements; the resident untied head is never computed. No whole-training speedup is established.','', 'The superseded manual-gradient results remain byte-preserved in [historical Markdown](embedding-component-results-manual-history.md) and [historical JSON](embedding-component-results-manual-history.json). Their owner runs are not final acceptance evidence.','', '## Setup and scope','', 'Eight H100 80GB ranks, one dense NCCL shard group; V=128256, D=4096, B=2, S=4096 (8192 tokens/rank), FP32 owner masters/returned shard gradient, native BF16 lookup/source coalescing and BF16 payloads. The actual untied FP32 lm_head and 2,101,346,304-byte private gradient bucket remain resident in both variants. No separate owner scratch pool or allocating fallback was observed; every owner rank borrows that bucket.','', 'Each case uses two warmups and three unprofiled samples. A table median is the median of the three sample-wise slowest-rank spans. The displayed range is max minus min, not an uncertainty estimate. Baseline runs are reused unchanged: `baseline-fixture-001`, `baseline-integrated-001`, `baseline-phases-001`. Final owner runs are `owner-standard-{integrated,phases,stages}-001`; all exited 0 with eight rank receipts. Every per-rank signed-int64 input hash, route census, shape, head residency, fixture index and unchanged active GFSDP file hash matches its baseline.','', '## Integrated component forward + backward','', '| Case | Baseline wall ms (range) | Final owner wall ms (range) | Median wall change | Allocated peak GiB, base → owner | Reserved peak GiB, base → owner |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
