lines+=['', 'These are application bytes summed over all eight ranks, not physical fabric traffic. Each owner contributes a 72-byte count vector; each rank explicitly reads its 576-byte gathered count matrix once/forward (4608 logical bytes across ranks). This is not the only inherited synchronization: MCP also observes a pinned DtoH and `cudaStreamSynchronize` in `partition_ids`, alongside the count-stage pageable DtoH. Native unique/sorting dynamic-output work remains on the affected path.','', 'The unchanged baseline logically gathers a 1,050,673,152-byte BF16 full table in forward and again in backward, then reduce-scatters a 2,101,346,304-byte FP32 full gradient. Owner traffic replaces those payloads with routed rows plus count metadata.','', '## Bounded MCP Perfetto mechanism evidence','', f"All **16** new canonical plain-JSON traces were loaded with MCP `load_trace`, then queried with `execute_sql`. Exact raw/imported X-event category counts match on every trace, including all kernels, GPU copies/memsets and overlapping GPU annotations; no normalization or timestamp rewriting was necessary. Total raw size is {sum(t['bytes'] for t in traces):,} bytes. One extra complete F+B/case/rank was profiled outside timing samples (one microbatch/rank, below the three-microbatch bound). [SQL, compact results and trace handles](embedding-component-perfetto.json) retain the queries; [primary JSON](embedding-component-results.json) pins all trace paths/hashes.", '', 'Source → CPU range → CUDA runtime/driver launch → device flow establishes the following for fixture and skew on all eight ranks:', '', '- `partition_ids`: signed-int64 native sort/unique/reduction kernels and DtoD/pinned DtoH work; `counts`: one metadata NCCL AllGather and one pageable DtoH. The one AllGather is the 72-byte local count vector / 576-byte output, not an embedding table gather.', '- `request_exchange`, `value_exchange`, `gradient_exchange`: exactly one `ncclDevKernel_SendRecv` each, tied by launch flow to the corresponding `all_to_all_single` context; three routed transports per rank/case.', '- `owner_lookup` and `reconstruct`: native gather/copy kernels; native BF16 `compute_grad_weight<c10::BFloat16, long>` and `sum_and_scatter<c10::BFloat16, long>` occur in source coalescing, followed by gathered unique rows.', '- `owner_reduction`: per-source BF16-to-FP32 copies and FP32 indexed accumulation; standard autograd subsequently accumulates the owned returned gradient. There is no full-table owner AllGather or ReduceScatter device kernel in any trace.', '', 'Profile durations are mechanism evidence and include rank-arrival/profiler perturbation. For example fixture rank 0 spends 14.496 ms in count-stage `cudaMemcpyAsync`, paired with a 14.540 ms metadata NCCL kernel; this is a wait-containing profiled span, not the unprofiled count-stage cost. Do not use it as a general communication bandwidth or CPU cost estimate.','', '| Profile, rank 0 | Non-NCCL kernel sum ms | NCCL kernel sum ms | Copy sum ms | Memset sum ms | Device interval union ms | Device first-to-last span ms |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
